# Binding: steward-gpt-oss-20b (one way, not the way)

The reference implementation's binding: `steward:1`, an Ollama model built from `gpt-oss:20b`
with a 65536-token context window, on one 16 GB GPU. It is **one example of a binding**. It is not a
default and not a requirement. Any model that provides what a profile requires can wear that
profile, on any runtime (Ollama or an OpenAI-compatible server), on any hardware. Run the
conformance kit with your own binding to see which profiles pass on your machine.

A binding is runtime config. It is never part of a board, and no profile or task names one. It
is the one place a model, an endpoint and a machine are named. Results are reported against it.

```json
{
  "stew": "2026-11-08-draft",
  "kind": "binding",
  "name": "steward-gpt-oss-20b",
  "api": "ollama",
  "endpoint": "http://127.0.0.1:11434",
  "model": "steward:1",
  "provides": {
    "tool_calling": true,
    "context": 65536,
    "structured_output": true,
    "reasoning_effort": true
  },
  "hardware": "one 16 GB GPU",
  "options": {
    "num_ctx": 65536,
    "keep_alive": "30m"
  }
}
```
